<%# Mean/Median/Mode/Range result (spec issue #80, DESIGN.md §4 Hero-result + Stat grid).
    Regenerated from the spec against the updated BLEND system — the headline change is the
    **responsive auto-fit stat grid** (DESIGN.md §4 "Stat grid"): the stat cards size to a
    min width and flow/wrap (no pinned column count), ~4 across on a wide results panel and
    collapsing to 2×2 when narrow. Each card's min width + padding is set so even a large
    (6+ digit) sum or count fits without clipping or overflow — the worst case the §-spec
    explicitly calls out.

    A surface card with a 5px coral left rule holds the eight descriptive statistics:
      • `mode` leads on its own full-width row because its value is an ARRAY (the deliberate
        non-scalar output, spec #80): the helper phrases it "23 and 38" (multimodal), a
        single value, or "No mode" (all values unique) — never an arbitrary number. The
        "No mode" sentinel reads in `faint` and carries an explicit caption, so the empty
        case is conveyed by text + weight, not colour alone (DESIGN.md §6).
      • mean / median / range — the central-tendency + spread headline figures, big
        tabular-nums in the auto-fit grid.
      • sum / count / smallest / largest — the supporting figures, a quieter auto-fit row
        under a thin rule.

    `calc:` is a valid Calculators::MeanMedianModeRange; the result keys are the eight in
    ARCHITECTURE.md §4. %>
<% mode = calc.result[:mode] %>
<div class="overflow-hidden rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)]">
  <div class="flex gap-5 p-7">
    <%# The 5px coral left rule (DESIGN.md §4 Hero-result). %>
    <span class="w-[5px] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
      <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent">Descriptive statistics</p>

      <%# Mode — its own headline row. The array is phrased by the helper ("23 and 38" / a
          single value / "No mode"). A real mode reads in ink tabular-nums; the "No mode"
          sentinel reads in faint AND names itself in the caption, so the empty case is
          signalled by text + de-emphasis, never colour alone (DESIGN.md §6). %>
      <dl class="mt-3">
        <dt class="text-xs font-bold text-label">Mode</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 break-words text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.03em] tabular-nums <%= mode.empty? ? "text-faint" : "text-ink" %>">
          <%= mmr_mode_display(mode) %>
        </dd>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-[11px] leading-snug text-faint">
          <%= mode.empty? ? "Every value occurs once — no value repeats" : "Most frequent value#{"s" if mode.many?}" %>
        </dd>
      </dl>

      <%# Mean / Median / Range — the headline figures in the shared responsive stat grid
          (DESIGN.md §4 "Stat grid", issue #143): `.stat-grid` / `.stat-card` size each card
          to a min width and let the grid flow, collapsing as the panel narrows. The card
          shell comfortably holds a 6+ digit tabular-nums figure. %>
      <dl class="mt-5 stat-grid">
        <% mmr_primary_stats.each do |stat| %>
          <div class="stat-card">
            <dt class="text-xs font-bold text-label"><%= stat[:label] %></dt>
            <dd class="mt-1.5 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.03em] tabular-nums text-ink">
              <%= mmr_stat_display(calc.result[stat[:key]]) %>
            </dd>
            <p class="mt-1 text-[11px] leading-snug text-faint"><%= stat[:caption] %></p>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </dl>

      <%# Supporting figures — sum / count / smallest / largest. The same shared responsive
          track (`.stat-grid`, issue #143) under a thin rule (DESIGN.md §4 Data table rules),
          but deliberately CARD-LESS: a quieter supporting row of bare label-over-value
          figures (no `.stat-card` shell), so it reads as a footnote to the headline cards
          above rather than a second card row. The shared track still sizes each figure to
          the canonical min width and flows, so a large count or sum never clips. %>
      <dl class="mt-6 stat-grid border-t border-rule pt-5">
        <% mmr_supporting_stats.each do |stat| %>
          <div class="min-w-0">
            <dt class="text-xs font-bold text-label"><%= stat[:label] %></dt>
            <dd class="mt-1 break-words text-lg font-bold tracking-[-0.01em] tabular-nums text-ink">
              <%= mmr_stat_display(calc.result[stat[:key]]) %>
            </dd>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
